WEBVTT

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:07.960
<b>United Kingdom of Arandas: Near the Border</b>

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:23.500
<b>Ingelmia Army: Northwestern Theater Frontline Forces</b>

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.890
Our allies have begun the attack!

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:32.580
Hurry!

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.320
Yes, sir!

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.220
The United Kingdom of Arandas

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.280
and the National Federation of Ingelmia

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.730
are fighting for control of the continent.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:46.070
Arandas possesses rich natural resources,

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:49.790
but Ingelmia has expanded to the south,
absorbing the nations in its path

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:53.740
and increasing its military might.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:56.390
In a series of defeats,

00:00:56.390 --> 00:01:00.890
Arandas has been pushed back
to the vicinity of its borders.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.570
The defenses on its Great Wall are powerful,

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.920
and Ingelmia has failed
several times to cross it.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.750
The battle seemed to be
drawing to a stalemate.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.570
Encounter

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:16.720
Enemy forces are massing.
Encounter

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:16.760
Enemy forces are massing.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.070
There is no need to worry.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:25.480
The Great Wall has protected us from
barbarians since Arandas's founding.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.070
What need is there to worry?

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:30.400
It's just as you say.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.900
Our country has a long and glorious history.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:38.140
We're here to perform an inspection,
so the timing is perfect:

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:41.290
tell the troops to drive them off.

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:41.870
Yes, sir.

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:51.710
Sorry to have you do this
at a time like this.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.250
You have my sympathies.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.190
The generals will be on their way soon.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:57.790
Yes, but...

00:01:58.690 --> 00:01:59.940
I won't let them get in the way.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:02.800
Their goal is to rally the troops.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:03.560
Yes, sir.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:05.540
Thanks.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:06.270
Not at all.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.540
What exactly is this war?

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:13.760
An invasion?

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:15.780
A conquest?

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:19.200
No, this is liberation!

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:24.830
The enemy nation is wealthy,
but do its citizens live happily?

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.830
No!

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.530
What are those?

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.160
And why is that?

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:58.850
The rulers of that nation hoard
the wealth for themselves,

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:02.950
and make war so that they line
their pockets and grow fat!

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.220
Fight, men!

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.170
Save Arandas!

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:14.170
Release our neighbors' land and
people from their corrupt rulers!

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:17.000
This is a war of liberation!

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.510
Liberation, eh?

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.310
It's all in how you say it, huh?

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:24.780
You're brave enough to say that.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.690
I should take a lesson from you.

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:27.890
Maybe.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:30.700
The Bloody Hopper squad has made it inside.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.020
We'll head for the main gate.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.960
Don't forget to provide support.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:49.540
Just wait a little longer.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.070
It'll be done soon.

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:51.990
Hot!

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:55.470
Lorenz, don't take the dressing out first!

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:56.290
Why?

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:59.800
With that type of rations you put
the rice on the plate and steam it.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.840
If you open the dressing while it's cooking
it'll be at just the right temperature!

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:04.930
I see.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.510
It doesn't change, does it?

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:07.080
Yup.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:07.720
It's the same.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.810
Fools! That's why you—

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.740
Yeah, yeah, we get it.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:14.030
I don't care, just hurry!

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:15.480
We're starving here.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.130
You guys, too!

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.620
You need to be stay disciplined!

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.380
We get it.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:22.420
Lorenz-san, Hikaru, hurry!

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:23.010
Right!

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.570
Give it to me. I'll do it!

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.780
Captain Samonji.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:44.090
Lunch is ready.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:45.720
Suzushiro.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:50.310
I know they've just unpacked, but...

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:53.810
They're going to hate you.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.810
I'm used to it.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:09.700
Independent Squad 8 will
now abandon this fortress.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.620
We're moving out immediately.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:12.790
We're leaving behind the large vehicles.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:14.390
Get together food, weapons, ammo.

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:16.790
Everything you can carry! Hurry!

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.260
Why did it have to be so sudden?

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:25.380
Tokimune!

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.680
Stop eating and get going!

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:27.970
Right!

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.560
You could've at least let me eat lunch!

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.560
Akane, when your hands are free take this!

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.760
Noobie, we're ready!

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:37.900
I'm Tokimune!

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.440
Thank you!

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.080
We just got here, too!

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:42.470
What're you going on about?

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:43.840
The orders? The food?

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:44.480
Both...

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:46.490
I mean, nothing!

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:51.360
Was the food good?

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:52.190
Y-Yes.

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:53.340
It was.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:55.840
That's great.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:58.110
At least you got a little something to eat

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:00.130
and now we've started the new mission.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.110
One job after another.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:04.880
You need to have the right
mentality to be happy.

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:07.880
Mentality?

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.300
Yup. Your mentality is
important on the battlefield.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.850
Well, see you.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.110
Silfy, Lorenz,

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:33.420
Tokimune, leave as soon as you're ready.

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:36.620
Roger.

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:39.250
Okay!

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:35.120
Don't break the formation!

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:37.470
Can't you even make your machine walk?

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:38.460
I'm doing it!

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:39.810
You are not!

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:42.630
Roger! I will ensure that my
machine walks properly!

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:44.070
What's with the sass?!

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:47.740
Our pilots are amusing.

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:48.750
Indeed.

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:13.090
Please wait, Generals!

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:14.930
We'll take command from the rear!

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:18.190
The soldiers are waiting
for your encouragement.

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:20.100
We need you out there, now!

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.940
The battlefield should be run by those present there.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:25.980
We're simply here for an inspection.

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:26.780
But...

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:29.330
We cannot die here.

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:31.400
You understand that, Izumi.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.880
We must return to the northwestern base

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:36.680
and devise a counterattack
as soon as possible.

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:37.780
Listen, Colonel.

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.410
We're going to win this, no matter what.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:45.260
Tell everyone to defend
this base down to the last man.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:54.300
Colonel.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.140
Telegraph all forces!

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:09.290
It's fallen.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:10.610
The Great Wall?

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:14.610
The old men are doing their
best to cause chaos down there.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:16.830
And we're badly outnumbered.

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:19.110
We can't win.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:22.890
I've received an encoded
message from our allies.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:25.950
"Live, and return to the
Gate of No Retreat," right?

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:27.290
That's right.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.510
That sounds like a decision he would make.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:30.950
Colonel Izumi?

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:32.550
Withdraw?

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:34.860
Are we running, then?

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:37.870
What, you didn't know that
while you were walking here?

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:41.810
Then what about our fellow soldiers?

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:46.140
If we weren't out in the middle
of nowhere we could've saved them.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:49.060
Why do you think we were out there?

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:51.310
They don't like us, or something?

00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:52.080
Yup.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:53.570
You're pretty smart.

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:56.270
But...

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:57.970
Are you some kind of hero?

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:01.830
No...

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:05.070
Even if we did go, what could we do?

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:06.740
Not a damn thing.

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:11.000
We just need to keep our mouths shut
and do what the captain tells us.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:11.900
Yup.

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:14.980
Just follow him, and we're good.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:18.810
You can start thinking about that
stuff once you're a real soldier.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:20.300
I already <i>am</i> a real soldier!

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:22.090
Break time is over.

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:26.380
I want two Trail Kriegers
in front and Seeker backup.

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:27.300
Understood.

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:36.270
It all worked out, huh? We're moving out, Noobie!

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:37.400
My name is Tokimune!

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:38.410
Ooh, scary!

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:39.410
He's mad.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:41.870
Go work off some of that stress.

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:10.770
Keep an eye on our surroundings.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:11.790
Yes, ma'am!

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:22.940
Wow, Chief... You sure know a lot!

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:25.440
There's no water in the valley up ahead.

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:27.520
So it sometimes served as a supply line.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.940
It was used to transport materials,

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:31.630
but it wasn't very convenient.

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:33.560
I don't know if it's been used recently, though.

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:34.920
I see.

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:42.560
Before you were born, that was a river.

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:49.980
But everything's changed.

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:52.630
It brings back a lot of memories.

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:04.910
Captain, I'm seeing destroyed
vehicles on our route.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:07.910
They're under attack from someone.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:08.580
Roger.

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:10.410
Is this area already under Ingelmian control?

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.090
No, it's too soon.

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:13.080
Shall I bring the two Trail Krieger back?

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:16.980
We won't change our route.

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:18.830
The main force will stay
on standby temporarily.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:23.360
Silfy and Tokimune will go on
ahead and confirm the situation.

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:24.300
Roger.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.100
Did you hear that, Tokimune?

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:26.800
Yes.

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:29.040
We'll circle around through the mountains.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:30.330
Don't trip.

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:31.540
I know.

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:32.940
I learned how to do it at school.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:34.510
This isn't a classroom.

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:36.530
That's right. Be careful.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:47.390
Is he gonna be okay?

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:49.060
No clue.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:23.840
Gunfire up ahead.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:24.620
Stop.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:29.040
I can hear the vehicles approaching.

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:30.860
Any allied troops in the vicinity?

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:32.490
None that I can see.

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:39.660
They're heading toward you.

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:40.610
Roger.

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:41.770
Stay put, Tokimune.

00:13:41.770 --> 00:13:42.340
Right.

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.670
Civilians?

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.920
A civilian trailer and unknown
armored car are under attack.

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:27.780
They're being chased by an Ingelmia
trailer and two Trail Kriegers.

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:28.950
Roger.

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:32.220
We need to meet up with the
main forces immediately.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:34.710
We don't have time to waste
on unnecessary battles.

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:36.330
An enemy trap?

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:38.090
That's one possibility.

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:39.400
Wait a second!

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:41.740
Are we just going to let the civilians die, then?!

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:43.390
Armed civilians?

00:14:43.390 --> 00:14:44.670
The risk is too great.

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:45.990
But if they're really...

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:46.490
Tokimune!
But if they're really...

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:47.020
Tokimune!

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:51.740
I can't put our troops in danger for an "if."

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:53.490
That's an order,

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:54.750
Private Susumu.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.750
Minakata-san! Minakata-san!

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:09.480
Let's keep an eye on our surroundings,

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:11.510
and find the optimal route.

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:12.290
Roger.

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:19.780
Hey, Tokimune!

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:24.060
What are you doing?

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:26.340
If you don't want to put your
troops at risk, I'll go!

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:27.430
You idiot!

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:35.910
These Trail Kriegers are so slow!

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.510
What was it?

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:55.180
Hurry! Hurry, Jamie!

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:03.690
Damn it, I screwed up!

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:10.980
I knew it! They're civilians!

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:27.210
Why am I always like this?

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:30.960
Hang in there, Tokimune!

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:33.590
Hang on for ten more seconds!

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:34.720
I'm not going to make it!

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:51.450
I know! I know, but...

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:57.130
Hey! You need to run!

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:01.230
You idiot!

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:03.120
There's no way I can run!

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:05.980
What the hell did you hit me for?

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:07.810
My life's on the line here too!

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:10.350
Not that you military bastards
would ever understand that!

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:12.960
I'm here to save you.

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:14.700
You can be a little nicer!

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:32.730
Hey, you!

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:39.200
What is this?

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:41.180
Argevollen Stablis Prima.

00:17:42.210 --> 00:17:43.580
Arge-what?

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:45.730
It's better than them taking it.

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:46.990
It's better than getting killed!

00:17:46.990 --> 00:17:47.530
Hey!

00:17:47.530 --> 00:17:49.590
I'm piloting it! I'll use it to get out of here!

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:51.890
If you knew how to use it,
why didn't you just do that in the first place?

00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:52.630
Fight!

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:54.800
I can't!

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:56.440
I can't...

00:17:57.210 --> 00:17:59.010
but I have to!

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:07.710
Here it is!

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:15.120
Argevollen device call.

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:17.780
Starting system boot-up sequence.

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:19.780
Jamie Hazaford.

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:23.670
ID Number 06120530.

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:26.290
Transcription: Jamie Hazaford.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:36.800
What?

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:38.550
I know!

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:41.900
You fight! You're a pilot, after all!

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:42.930
Okay!

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:45.070
Nice idea! Nice going, me!

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:47.970
You want me to pilot it?

00:18:47.970 --> 00:18:48.600
Please.

00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:04.970
Reinforcements, huh?

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:06.240
Hey, what do I do?!

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:07.780
Boot it up and fight!

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:08.830
That's not what I meant!

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:10.590
What's the boot up process?

00:19:10.590 --> 00:19:11.960
What checks should I prioritize?

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:13.780
What weapons do I have?

00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:14.870
Wait a second.

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:19.500
Boot process... cheese?

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:19.970
Here it is!

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:21.470
Grab the lever!

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:21.890
Huh?!

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:22.990
Just do it!

00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:46.790
What?

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:57.260
Listen,

00:19:57.260 --> 00:20:01.470
just envision in your head
what you want to do next.

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:05.850
Keep your focus and don't
act out of instinct!

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.000
Envision?

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:34.260
